{{also|Pfeifen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{der|de|gmh|pfīfen}}, {{der|de|goh|phīfōn}}, from onomatopoeic {{der|de|la|pīpāre}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈpfaɪ̯fən/|[ˈpfaɪ̯fən]|[pfaɪ̯fɱ̩]|lang=de}} {{a|standard}}
* {{IPA|/ˈfaɪ̯fən/|lang=de}} {{a|most speakers in northern and central Germany}}
* {{audio|De-pfeifen.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=1|pfeift|pfiff|gepfiffen|past subjunctive=pfiffe}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive|or|transitive}} to [[whistle]] (with one's mouth or a whistle)
#: {{ux|de|Hör auf zu '''pfeifen'''!|Stop '''whistling'''!|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|de|Er '''pfeift''' ein Liedchen.|He's '''whistling''' a song.|inline=1}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|or|transitive|sports}} to act as [[referee]]
#: {{ux|de|Der Schiedsrichter '''pfeift''' sehr gut.|The referee is doing a great job.|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|de|Wer '''pfeift''' das Spiel?|Who's '''refereeing''' the game?|inline=1}}
# {{lb|de|colloquial|intransitive|_|with preposition [[auf]]}} to be [[uninterested]] (in something or someone); to [[ignore]]; not to [[give a damn]]
#: {{ux|de|Darauf '''pfeif''' ich!|I don't care one bit about that!|inline=1}}

